 !!! Note
     The minimum last stake amount can be configured using `last_stake_amount_min_ratio` - which defaults to 0.5 (50%). This means that the minimum stake amount that's ever used is `stake_amount * 0.5`. This avoids very low stake amounts, that are close to the minimum tradable amount for the pair and can be refused by the exchange.
 
+#### Underlying currency exposure limit
+
+If you trade several pairs that are all priced against (or margined in) the same underlying currency - e.g. several USDT-quoted pairs, or a handful of BTC-margined futures - a large adverse move in that one currency can hit several of your open trades at once.
+
+`max_underlying_currency_exposure` lets you cap, per strategy, what fraction of your total tradable capital may be committed at the same time to trades sharing a pair's quote currency. When opening (or adjusting) a trade would push the combined stake for that currency above the configured fraction, the stake amount is reduced to whatever room is left, or the trade is skipped entirely if there's no room left (the same way other stake-sizing limits are already resolved). The reason is logged just like other entry-sizing decisions, and this behaves identically in live/dry-run and in backtesting, since both run through the same sizing logic.
+
+```json
+"max_underlying_currency_exposure": 0.5
+```
+
+With the configuration above, no more than 50% of your tradable capital may ever be committed at once to trades sharing the same underlying currency.
+
+!!! Note
+    Since Freqtrade requires all pairs in a single bot instance to share the same quote currency, this setting most commonly acts as an overall cap on simultaneously committed capital for that strategy - distinct from, and applied in addition to, `tradable_balance_ratio`.
+
 #### Static stake amount
 
 The `stake_amount` configuration statically configures the amount of stake-currency your bot will use for each trade.
